WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:06.550
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this is my
Korra Episode 5 video.

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:09.870
Kuvira turned a big corner and Korra is back
in action.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.670
It’s like the eye of the storm.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.360
Korra went through hell to fix herself, now
it’s that really pregnant pause before everything

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.920
goes insane again.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.010
Quick reminder, new round of the giveaway
starts now, all you have to do to enter is

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.460
be a subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.410
Careful for spoilers if you’re not caught
up.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.733
Zhu Li, do the Top 5 moments thing.

00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:29.439
I really need to hire a zhu li of my own.

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:31.070
Number 5 - Varrick’s Superweapon

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.719
I’m totally not suprised it turned out to
be a weapon of mass destruction.

00:00:34.719 --> 00:00:39.820
Varrick’s speechifying reminded me of the
original Manhattan Project.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.539
Especially with the way he was filming himself,
chronicling his progress.

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:46.280
You can think of this as a wink back at the
movers from book 2.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:50.870
We got all the Nuktuk stuff in book 3 so maybe
when they’re all done Bolin will retire

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.980
and start making them again.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:57.379
The animation effect on it looked just like
the energy blasts Korra and UnaVaatu were

00:00:57.379 --> 00:00:59.149
giving off during the book 2 finale.

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:02.890
Varrick has accidentally replicated the power
of energy benders in a way.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.950
Energy Bending is way more complicated than
just blasting people.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:13.920
But it’s capable of causing Avatar levels
of Destruction.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.240
That does not make Kuvira the new Dark Avatar
though.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:31.700
But I would pay good money to see that Cosplay.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.399
Who else was proud of Varrick for trying to
put the brakes on it too.

00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:37.450
I think we all knew what was going to happen
the minute the blast went off.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.450
Kuvira would try to take advantage of it.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.570
For now he’s stuck working on it.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:40.762
Mixed up in all this is the Varrick Zhu-Li
subplot.

00:01:40.762 --> 00:01:41.762
Which of course leads me to

00:01:41.762 --> 00:01:42.762
Number 4 - Zhu Li Turns a big corner

00:01:42.762 --> 00:01:47.170
Korra and Kuvira are the two lead characters
in the episode, but Zhu Li was the biggest

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.170
badass.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:51.780
And yes, I know everyone is wondering what’s
up with her turning sides at the end.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:52.899
I think that’s all bullcrap.

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:56.880
She’s already shown herself to be smarter
and a better fighter than Varrick, so it stands

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.420
to reason that she’s also better at manipluation.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.829
I think she just said all that so that she
could stay and protect Varrick.

00:02:02.829 --> 00:02:06.880
I am hoping they’ll have some fun with the
character and make her pretend to be bad for

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.468
another episode or two before she saves Varrick
again and helps him escape.

00:02:08.468 --> 00:02:10.280
She also got the best line in the episode.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:14.630
They gave her Varrick’s line “Guards Do
The Thing!”

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:19.390
She and Varrick have a weird relationship,
the almost kiss was high on my list too.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:22.360
I think they’ll seal the deal before the
end of the season.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.800
Number 3 - Suyin’s Flashback

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:29.240
It’s nice they included this, I think we
all had a pretty good idea of what went down

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:30.960
between them though.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.270
They had that scene back in Republic City
where Kuvira called her out for sitting on

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.110
her butt when the Earth Kingdom was in chaos.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:40.990
I actually thought explaining what was up
with P’tar Junior’s crazy hate of his

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.070
family was all about.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.780
He was nuts in this episode.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:45.850
Even Kuvira had to tell him to chill.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:50.220
She told Suyin she didn’t brainwash him,
which of course means she brainwashed the

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.620
crap out of him.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.370
Not Dai Li brainwashed, she just whispered
in his ear.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:56.370
She’s also probably using all the sex they’re
having to cloud his judgement.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.370
I know we haven’t seen any Kuvira sex scenes.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:58.370
Even though I’m sure they exist on tumblr.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.370
But just because they haven’t shown them
doesn’t mean no one is having sex.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.370
I’m sure the world of Avatar is very traditional,
but you heard Kuvira, “she always gets what

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:01.370
she wants.”

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:02.370
That’s not important to the episode, I just
think it’s funny to pry open the characters

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.370
lives when we don’t see them on screen.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:04.370
Number 2 - Kuvira is pours Bolin all of the
Metal Kool-Aide

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.370
For those that don’t get the kool-aide reference,
there was a crazy religious cult a long time

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.370
ago that brainwashed all the members and made
them drink poisoned kool-aide in this weird

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.370
suicide ritual.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.370
Of course Bolin figures out what’s going
on.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.370
There’s no way we’re going to start the
second half of the season without Team Korra

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.500
all being on the same side.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.950
I know Mako and Asami are back in Republic
City but we still have another couple weeks

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.350
before we pass the halfway mark.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:19.120
I was surprised they didn’t do much with
Bolin during the negotiation.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:24.130
He did have that speech but the minute Kuvira
walked in the door Suyin already had her mind

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:29.830
made up, so it was all pointless.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:33.430
The Mech Battle was amazing.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:35.510
The trailer didn’t do it justice.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:38.250
Zhu Li has been holding out on us.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.700
She isn’t a bender but I see her as an Asami
character.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.140
Someone who is really smart and a good fighter.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.900
So of course she can pilot the mech.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:49.030
If you didn’t catch it, Bryke explained
during Comic Con that the Mechs look different

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.400
based on the rank they are.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.400
Like military ranks.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.890
So I believe the Green ones are of a higher
rank.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:55.570
I think they’re all the same structurally
though.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:58.960
We also learned Lava Bending is very effective
against them.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.360
The mintue Bolin lava bended those two they
went down instantly.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.490
So just remember that.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:05.920
It’s like Mako lightning bending Ming Hua
in book 3.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:07.050
Just instant takedown.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:12.990
As for the re-education camps, don’t you
feel like the Dai Li would be the camp counselors

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:13.990
there.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:14.990
Re-education of course being brainwashing.

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:15.990
When Kuvira said she was sending Zhu-Li there
too all I could think of was Joo De.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.900
I think there names being so similar sounding
is just a coincidence though.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:22.590
and my Number 1 moment - Korra and Kuvira
get ready to throw down.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.410
Korra gave her a chance, now it’s time to
kick some butt.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.710
After she saves Suyin and her sons.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.100
That was the big WTF at the end.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:36.469
Suyin had taken her twin sons and it sounded
like they were going to capture Kuvira.

00:04:36.469 --> 00:04:38.639
Potentially very bad PR move.

00:04:38.639 --> 00:04:40.870
Kuvira is playing it smart.

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:43.050
She even said all the world’s eyes are on
us.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.800
So Suyin attacking will be all she needs to
launch a full scale assault.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.939
I love how Suyin treated Korra kind of like
Zhu Li too.

00:04:50.939 --> 00:04:53.419
Korra do the Avatar thing.

00:04:53.419 --> 00:04:57.530
Theoretically Korra would be able to earthbend
a giant hand to just swat all the mechs like

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.530
flies.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:02.819
But she and Kuvira had such a classic Gunslinger
standoff I feel like it would be a huge bummer

00:05:02.819 --> 00:05:05.389
if they didn’t face off against each other.

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:09.949
That wouldn’t be the smartest way to defeat
her, Korra needs to learn to play the game

00:05:09.949 --> 00:05:10.949
of thrones.

00:05:10.949 --> 00:05:12.409
She needs Cersei Lannister to teach her politics.

00:05:12.409 --> 00:05:16.039
Also it didn’t really fit into my top 5
moments, but Asami with her father was really

00:05:16.039 --> 00:05:17.039
big.

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:21.400
The actor that plays Hiroshi Sato said he
came back to do scenes a long time ago, so

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.400
we knew he was going to be here.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.449
We just didn’t know what his role would
be.

00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:28.849
It seems like based on what’s going on between
P’tar Junior and his father, Asami’s scenes

00:05:28.849 --> 00:05:31.889
were all about healing family relationships
and forgiveness.

00:05:31.889 --> 00:05:35.199
That’s going to be a big throughline for
all the characters this season.

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:36.199
Forgiveness.

00:05:36.199 --> 00:05:38.454
So just remember that when it comes time for
a final battle between Korra and Kuvira in

00:05:38.454 --> 00:05:41.509
the last couple of episodes.

00:05:41.509 --> 00:05:44.510
Forgive each other and play some pai sho.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:48.500
And maybe cry a little because this is the
last season.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:52.539
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and do you think everyone will be able to

00:05:52.539 --> 00:05:55.680
forgive Kuvira after she goes crazy with that
superweapon.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.659
I felt like it was heavily implied that Kuvira
would use it and that would be the minute

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:04.779
the world turns on her.

00:06:04.779 --> 00:06:09.000
You don’t place a gun on the table before
a fight if you don’t plan on using it.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:14.110
If any of you are theater geeks, there’s
this thing called Chekov’s Gun, “One must

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:17.229
never place a rifle on the stage if it’s
not going to go off.”

00:06:17.229 --> 00:06:21.249
- so just plan on that giant spirit vine rifle
going off

00:06:21.249 --> 00:06:22.889
Which is actually a good transition to my
review.

00:06:22.889 --> 00:06:28.870
I gave the episode an A just because it was
such a big turning point for all the characters

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:36.050
and in the shuffle they focused on very under-developed
characters.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:38.310
Zhu Li just got so much more interesting.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:44.009
P’tar Junior is the whiny son with no self-esteem,
so yes, it’s annoying to listen to him whine

00:06:44.009 --> 00:06:46.409
about how hard it was growing up rich and
famous.

00:06:46.409 --> 00:06:49.970
I’m sure all the poor people in Ba Sing
Se really give a shit about all that.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:55.569
I feel like if a character can’t be someone
you admire, they might as well be someone

00:06:55.569 --> 00:06:57.139
you can really really hate.

00:06:57.139 --> 00:07:00.680
That’s why I think Bryke wrote him being
so vicious in that Mech battle.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:02.719
If you’re going to be bad, be very bad.

00:07:02.719 --> 00:07:04.999
Don’t half ass being evil.

00:07:04.999 --> 00:07:08.400
Somewhere off in the distance Azula is laughing
at him.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:18.870
I’m totally not surprised when Korra episodes
are this good, I still think Toph and Korra

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.620
from episode 3 is the best episode so far.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.840
Mostly because it’s such fanservice.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:28.800
So Q&amp;A posting tomorrow morning.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.400
The Doctor Who Season finale is happening
then too so I’ll try to post that next Korra

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:32.400
video early.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.949
Sometimes I don’t finish it fast enough.

00:07:33.949 --> 00:07:35.199
Right now click here to get that.

00:07:35.199 --> 00:07:39.221
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post
it and Click here for Korra Episode 4.

00:07:39.221 --> 00:07:42.030
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and i’ll see you tonight!

